# comps groups unmarked when policy mode KIOSK is applied.
#
# Removing a package and leaving its comps group marked installed is the third of the three quiet
# ways a prune undoes itself (see policy-lib.sh, auros_unmark_groups). Nothing errors: the group
# simply stays marked, and the next `dnf group upgrade` in any later layer puts the desktop back.
#
# auros_unmark_groups tries both dnf verbs, then CHECKS, then warns loudly and records it in
# applied.json if a group is still marked. It does not pretend to have succeeded.
kde-desktop-environment
kde-desktop
kde-apps
kde-media
kde-office
gnome-desktop
